  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tampa Bay controlled this game from the second inning onward and the Athletics never recovered.",
    "what_this_means": "Perkins gave up six runs in five innings. Not the start this team needs right now. The bullpen did its job after, with Rom, Blewett, Juenger, and Johnson combining for four scoreless frames, but by then the game was already gone. Gelof hit two home runs and Butler added one, which would matter in most games. Not this one. They left runners on base in the first and second innings. Two critical moments when the deficit was still manageable. And that's where the game actually ended. Losing games when you put runners in scoring position and do nothing with them is not a new problem for this team. It's the problem getting louder.",
